<section
  class='fullscreen-section'
  id='about'
  data-title='About — Katja Turnsek | UX/UI Designer & Front-End Developer'
  data-description='UX/UI designer and front-end developer with a long professional background in art, visual communication, branding, and web design.'
>
  <div class='rows'>
    <div class='row'>
      <h1>About</h1>
      <h2>Design, UX, and the Code Behind It</h2>

      <p class='align-right-60'>
        I’m a
        <strong>UX/UI designer and front-end developer</strong>, but my working life began in
        <strong>visual design and art</strong>. That background still shapes how I approach digital
        work: I care about clear structure, thoughtful details, and giving each project its own
        visual character.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class='row'>
      <h3>My Story</h3>

      <p>
        I spent many years working as a professional artist and running my own creative business.
        Alongside that, I worked with branding, illustration, web design, touchscreen interfaces,
        and other forms of visual communication. Working directly with clients taught me how to
        listen, find the right direction, and turn an initial idea into something finished and
        useful.
      </p>

      <p>
        I later studied front-end development at Noroff because I wanted to do more than design how
        something should look, I wanted to build it too. Today, I work with
        <strong>HTML</strong>,
        <strong>CSS</strong>,
        <strong>JavaScript</strong>,
        <strong>TypeScript</strong>,
        <strong>React</strong>, and
        <strong>REST APIs</strong>
        to create responsive and accessible websites and interfaces.
      </p>

      <p>
        The part I enjoy most is where design and development meet. I can think through the
        structure and visual direction, work out how the experience should behave, and then turn it
        into a working interface. Understanding both sides also helps me make design decisions that
        work in practice, not only on a screen in Figma.
      </p>

      <p>
        When I’m not designing or coding, I paint
        <strong>fine-art pet portraits</strong>
        in oils. It may seem like very different work, but it requires much of the same patience,
        attention to detail, and care for the person on the other side.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class='row'>
      <h3>Skills at a Glance</h3>
    </div>

    <div class='animated-bars'>
      <div class='bar-stack'>
        <div class='bar bar-bg'></div>
        <div class='bar bar-1'>
          <span class='bar-label'>UX/UI DESIGN &amp; PROTOTYPING</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class='bar-stack'>
        <div class='bar bar-bg'></div>
        <div class='bar bar-2'>
          <span class='bar-label'>FRONT-END DEVELOPMENT</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class='bar-stack'>
        <div class='bar bar-bg'></div>
        <div class='bar bar-3'>
          <span class='bar-label'>VISUAL DESIGN &amp; BRANDING</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class='row'>
      <div class='demo-links'>
        <a
          href='https://github.com/KatjaTurnsek'
          target='_blank'
          class='label-link online-demo-label'
          rel='noopener'
        >
          <span class='label-text'>View GitHub</span>
          <svg class='icon icon-18 arrow-icon' aria-hidden='true'>
            <use href='#i-arrow-right' />
          </svg>
        </a>

        <a
          href='{{base}}#contact'
          class='label-link online-demo-label'
          aria-label='Go to contact section'
        >
          <span class='label-text'>Contact Me</span>
          <svg class='icon icon-18 arrow-icon' aria-hidden='true'>
            <use href='#i-arrow-right' />
          </svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class='testimonial-section'>
    <div class='testimonial'>
      <div class='testimonial-label'>
        <svg class='icon icon-14 arrow-icon' aria-hidden='true'>
          <use href='#i-arrow-down' />
        </svg>
        <h3 class='label-text'>Testimonials</h3>
      </div>

      <div class='circle-button'>
        <svg class='icon' aria-hidden='true'>
          <use href='#i-comment' />
        </svg>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class='rows'>
    <div class='row'>
      <figure class='testimonial-card'>
        <blockquote>
          “Katja is creative by nature and approaches every assignment with great dedication. Her
          work combines strong visual sense with clear structure, and she takes pride in delivering
          well-crafted, functional designs. Always positive, outgoing, and easy to collaborate with,
          a true professional and a pleasure to have on the team.”
        </blockquote>

        <figcaption>
          <span class='author'>Damjan Strucl</span>
          <span class='role'>CEO, Logina d.o.o</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <div class='row'>
      <figure class='testimonial-card'>
        <blockquote>
          “We are extremely happy with the logo and CD cover design created by Katja Turnsek. Her
